{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795268608245,"sessionID":"ses_e01a77fa2ffetYVuk2YIlLQx41","part":{"id":"prt_1fe58fe80001YcjOzGLD6YsNeT","messageID":"msg_1fe58aa25001hNOSG1B2BuRvTc","sessionID":"ses_e01a77fa2ffetYVuk2YIlLQx41","type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"read_3_e2656431","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/agnes/experiments/results-h1.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/agent/agnes/experiments/results-h1.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # H1 results\n2: \n3: ## Primary: text fulfillment (case-level)\n4: \n5: | arm | images | text hits/total | rate | Wilson 95% CI |\n6: |---|---|---|---|---|\n7: | prose | 50 | 601/620 | 0.969 | [0.953, 0.980] |\n8: | structured | 50 | 557/620 | 0.898 | [0.872, 0.920] |\n9: \n10: | primary metric | value |\n11: |---|---|\n12: | cases (paired) | 10 |\n13: | text fulfillment effect (structured - prose) | -7.9 pp |\n14: | bootstrap 95% CI | [-14.5, -2.6] pp |\n15: | permutation p (exact sign-flip) | 0.01562 |\n16: | GEE text_hits/text_total | OR=0.29 [0.19, 0.46], marginal=-7.4 pp, p=6.931e-08 |\n17: \n18: ## Key secondary: hard-gate pass (underpowered; hierarchical)\n19: \n20: | arm | images | passes | pass rate | Wilson 95% CI |\n21: |---|---|---|---|---|\n22: | prose | 50 | 6 | 0.120 | [0.056, 0.238] |\n23: | structured | 50 | 4 | 0.080 | [0.032, 0.188] |\n24: \n25: | secondary metric | value |\n26: |---|---|\n27: | hard-gate pass effect | -4.0 pp |\n28: | bootstrap 95% CI | [-18.0, 6.0] pp |\n29: | permutation p | 1 |\n30: | GEE pass ~ variant | OR=0.64 [0.24, 1.68], p=0.3616 |\n31: | McNemar p (b=0, c=1) | 1 |\n32: | power at 15pp, n=10 | 0.26 (do not read non-significance as no effect) |\n33: \n34: **Decision:** adopt=False (primary_pass=False, pass point estimate=-4.0 pp); held-out pass validation still required.\n35: \n36: ## Exploratory secondary outcomes (Holm)\n37: \n38: | outcome | effect (pp) | p | p_holm |\n39: |---|---|---|---|\n40: | requirement_fulfillment | -3.8 | 0.3242 | 0.9727 |\n41: | element_recall | 0.5 | 0.7656 | 1 |\n42: | text_exact | -24.0 | 0.03125 | 0.125 |\n43: | count_correct | -4.0 | 0.8281 | 1 |\n44: \n45: ## Per-case text fulfillment (after recheck corrections)\n46: \n47: | case | prose | structured | diff (pp) |\n48: |---|---|---|---|\n49: | 23 | 80/80 = 1.000 | 79/80 = 0.988 | -1.2 |\n50: | 153 | 70/70 = 1.000 | 69/70 = 0.986 | -1.4 |\n51: | 226 | 75/80 = 0.938 | 62/80 = 0.775 | -16.2 |\n52: | 270 | 45/45 = 1.000 | 43/45 = 0.956 | -4.4 |\n53: | 353 | 97/100 = 0.970 | 99/100 = 0.990 | +2.0 |\n54: | 371 | 10/10 = 1.000 | 10/10 = 1.000 | 0.0 |\n55: | 379 | 63/65 = 0.969 | 60/65 = 0.923 | -4.6 |\n56: | 387 | 74/75 = 0.987 | 64/75 = 0.853 | -13.3 |\n57: | 389 | 56/60 = 0.933 | 51/60 = 0.850 | -8.3 |\n58: | 475 | 31/35 = 0.886 | 20/35 = 0.571 | -31.4 |\n59: \n60: ## Scoring reliability (20% blind recheck)\n61: \n62: - 20 images (2 per case) were recoded from scratch with neutral filenames, without access to first-pass scores or arm labels.\n63: - Exact agreement: **15/20 (75%)**; mean absolute difference **0.35** text hits per image; max **2**.\n64: - Prose arm: 11/11 exact. Structured arm: 4/9 exact; every disagreement was in the structured arm and the first pass had been **too lenient** by 1-2 hits.\n65: - Corrections applied: case 226 captions are actually “朱高煦” and “朱厚熄” (verified at 3x on all 10 images), not “朱高炽/朱厚熜”; one case-23 image and one case-379 image were over-counted.\n66: - Effect of corrections: text-fulfillment gap moved from -7.1 pp to **-7.9 pp** (structured still worse), so the verdict is unchanged; hard-gate pass dropped from 22.0%/8.0% to 12.0%/8.0% because five prose passes lost the exact-text gate.\n67: - Remaining caveat: this is a same-rater temporal recheck, not a fully independent second rater. It measures consistency and catches legibility errors, not shared rater bias.\n68: \n69: ## Interpretation\n70: \n71: - H1 hypothesis (sectioned/structured prompt improves exact-text fulfillment) is **rejected**. Structured is 7.9 pp worse, bootstrap CI [-14.5, -2.6], exact sign-flip p = 0.0156; per-image GEE OR = 0.29 (p ≈ 7e-8).\n72: - Hard-gate pass is directionally consistent but underpowered; do not treat its non-significance as evidence of no effect.\n73: - The gap is concentrated: 475 (-31.4), 226 (-16.2), 387 (-13.3), 389 (-8.3); 353 is the only case favoring structured (+2.0), and 23/153/371 are near ceiling.\n74: - Failure pattern in the structured arm: dimension strings degrade to bare numbers (“高 180” → “180”), two-line captions collapse to one line (英宗 → “庙号”), and label blocks duplicate instead of binding one string per slot.\n75: - Decision per pre-registration: **do not adopt the structured writer**. Keep the prose contract as the production template.\n\n(End of file - total 75 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# H1 results\n\n## Primary: text fulfillment (case-level)\n\n| arm | images | text hits/total | rate | Wilson 95% CI |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| prose | 50 | 601/620 | 0.969 | [0.953, 0.980] |\n| structured | 50 | 557/620 | 0.898 | [0.872, 0.920] |\n\n| primary metric | value |\n|---|---|\n| cases (paired) | 10 |\n| text fulfillment effect (structured - prose) | -7.9 pp |\n| bootstrap 95% CI | [-14.5, -2.6] pp |\n| permutation p (exact sign-flip) | 0.01562 |\n| GEE text_hits/text_total | OR=0.29 [0.19, 0.46], marginal=-7.4 pp, p=6.931e-08 |\n\n## Key secondary: hard-gate pass (underpowered; hierarchical)\n\n| arm | images | passes | pass rate | Wilson 95% CI |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"actualStartLine":1,"actualLimit":75},"title":"workspace/agent/agnes/experiments/results-h1.md","time":{"start":1795268608215,"end":1795268608239}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795268609117,"sessionID":"ses_e01a77fa2ffetYVuk2YIlLQx41","part":{"id":"prt_1fe5900e3001Y1LS30Sz7qH7ng","messageID":"msg_1fe58aa25001hNOSG1B2BuRvTc","sessionID":"ses_e01a77fa2ffetYVuk2YIlLQx41","type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"read_4_22c7804b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/agent/agnes/experiments/results-h2.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/agent/agnes/experiments/results-h2.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # H2 pilot: in-image text vs post-hoc overlay\n2: \n3: ## Question\n4: \n5: For layouts with predictable caption bands, does generating a text-free image and\n6: overlaying text with PIL beat asking the image model to draw the text?\n7: \n8: ## Design (feasibility pilot, not a powered test)\n9: \n10: - Case 226 (2x4 imperial portrait grid, 16 text slots: 8 temple names + 8 personal names).\n11: - Arm A (control): H1 prose prompt with in-image text, 5 reps.\n12: - Arm B: same spec with `texts=[]` plus \"leave two blank caption lines\", 5 reps,\n13:   then PIL overlay using Noto Serif CJK SC Bold, centered on the detected blank band.\n14: - Same reference image for both arms; 1024x1024, `agnes-image-2.5-flash`.\n15: \n16: ## Manipulation check\n17: \n18: | arm | exact text slots | per-image exact | portraits | 4x2 grid |\n19: |---|---|---|---|---|\n20: | A in-image | 75/80 = 93.8% | 0/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 |\n21: | B overlay | 80/80 = 100% | 5/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 |\n22: \n23: - Arm A fails the same slot in all five images: 世宗 / 朱厚熜 is rendered as 朱厚熄.\n24: - Arm B text is constructed, so 100% is a manipulation check, not an independent win.\n25: \n26: ## Layout cost of overlay\n27: \n28: - Blank band was usable in **5/5** images; detected band height 100-167 px.\n29: - No text-on-portrait collision in **5/5**.\n30: - **1/5** (r6) had faint guide lines drawn inside the band by the model; overlay text\n31:   sits on those lines. Still legible, but it is a real integration defect.\n32: - Font is uniform Noto Serif; it reads cleaner but slightly less \"hand-painted\" than\n33:   the model's own lettering.\n34: \n35: ## Reading\n36: \n37: - When a layout has a clean, predictable caption band, overlay fixes the exact-text\n38:   failure at low structural cost. This is the strongest case for overlay.\n39: - It does not yet answer the harder layouts (475 dimension arrows, 387 UI, 389 bullets)\n40:   where text is entangled with structure and slots are not rectangular.\n41: - Decision: keep overlay as the candidate pipeline for caption-band layouts; do not\n42:   generalize until slot templates exist for the entangled layouts.\n43: \n44: ## Caveats\n45: \n46: - One case, n=5 per arm. Not powered; treat as feasibility evidence.\n47: - Arm B's text is deterministic, so text accuracy is not blind-comparable.\n48: - Overlay placement uses content-bottom detection plus manual inspection; production\n49:   would need a stable slot template.\n\n(End of file - total 49 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# H2 pilot: in-image text vs post-hoc overlay\n\n## Question\n\nFor layouts with predictable caption bands, does generating a text-free image and\noverlaying text with PIL beat asking the image model to draw the text?\n\n## Design (feasibility pilot, not a powered test)\n\n- Case 226 (2x4 imperial portrait grid, 16 text slots: 8 temple names + 8 personal names).\n- Arm A (control): H1 prose prompt with in-image text, 5 reps.\n- Arm B: same spec with `texts=[]` plus \"leave two blank caption lines\", 5 reps,\n  then PIL overlay using Noto Serif CJK SC Bold, centered on the detected blank band.\n- Same reference image for both arms; 1024x1024, `agnes-image-2.5-flash`.\n\n## Manipulation check\n\n| arm | exact text slots | per-image exact | portraits | 4x2 grid |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A in-image | 75/80 = 93.8% | 0/5 | 5/5 | 5/5 |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"actualStartLine":1,"actualLimit":49},"title":"workspace/agent/agnes/experiments/results-h2.md","time":{"start":1795268609092,"end":1795268609114}}}}
